[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-48", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 48 — LDBC's own short-read generator; the official column restated at 1773.1 ops/s (TCR 0.0002)", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-48.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 48 - LDBC's own short-read generator in the driver; the official column restated\n\n> Seed: iteration 47's S38. Judge: bench/benchmark.edn v2, `:schedule\n> :official`; rung :sf1-full; SUT levi (M4 4P+6E, 16 threads), driver\n> judah, LAN.\n\n## Generate / Rank\n\n  The generator was read from the LDBC driver's source\n  (LdbcSnbShortReadGenerator, LdbcSnbInteractiveWorkload) and ported as\n  it is: two id buffers replenished from every read's rows (which types\n  add which ids is a table in the source), a chain after each complex\n  read starting at probability 1.0 with a random first (person or\n  message short read), S1->S2->S3->S4->S5->S6->S7->S1..., a coin toss and\n  a buffer poll per step, the probability dropping by 0.2 after the last\n  person query and after the last message query, and each short read\n  scheduled at the previous operation's actual finish. Observed: ~6.4\n  short reads per complex read, against ~1 under iteration 46's\n  approximation.\n\n    schedule official, exact generator    tcr      on-time%  thru/s   upd/s  complex/s  short/s\n      64 slots                            0.0002    100.00   1773.1   1092      94        602   <- the row\n      64 slots                            0.00015    93.31   2009.1                              FAILS\n      128 slots                           0.00015    75.17   1975.0                              FAILS (deeper queue)\n\n  The official-column rows of iterations 46 and 47 (1360.9 at 0.00015,\n  1995.6 at 0.00012) were measured under the approximation; they are\n  marked superseded in the scoreboard and not compared to this row.\n\n## Reflect\n\n  - The row's number went DOWN in TCR and up in fidelity. That is the\n    right direction: a number under the benchmark's own generator is\n    worth more than a larger one under mine.\n  - At TCR 0.00015 the mix is ~2,400 ops/s with IC05 taking 2.9 of 16\n    threads; the failure is queueing, and more driver slots only deepen\n    the queue. What the receipts lack is on-time BY OP (S40): a failing\n    sweep should say which op was late.\n  - IC05 at 112 ms x 26/s remains the schedule's largest single cost\n    (S39); the host remains the ceiling under it.\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict under bench/benchmark.edn v2: the official column restated with\nthe exact generator (1773.1 at TCR 0.0002); earlier official rows\nsuperseded. Ratio to the audited No.1: 79 on throughput at a 16x slower\nTCR.\n\nSeeds for iteration 49, in order:\n\n  - S40: on-time by op in the receipt.\n  - S39: IC05's 112 ms under the schedule.\n  - S34: bindings as arrays. Owner: a SUT host.\n"}]
